<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  Windows application manifest for bacchus-fyne.exe (bacchus#136).

  It asks Windows for one thing and nothing else: run this process elevated.
  Device-wide routing on Windows needs it - creating the wintun adapter,
  New-NetRoute, New-NetIPAddress and the NetSecurity kill-switch are all
  administrator operations - and without this manifest nothing ever asked.
  A downloaded binary therefore launched unelevated, every connect failed at
  the first of those calls, and the only clue was one error string at the far
  end of the chain (bacchus#135).

  requireAdministrator rather than highestAvailable: a Bacchus that came up
  unelevated could not route this device at all, so every connect would refuse.
  An app that cannot do its one job is worse than a UAC prompt at launch, and
  the prompt is the accepted cost. It is not a silent one - unsigned, it says
  "Publisher: Unknown", which is bacchus#38's territory and deferred with it.

  Deliberately NOT here:

    - Common Controls v6. The retired tray client's bacchus.exe.manifest
      declared a dependency on Microsoft.Windows.Common-Controls 6.0.0.0
      because lxn/walk draws with comctl32 and renders as Windows 95 without
      it (docs/design/client-connection-ui.md). Fyne draws every widget itself
      through OpenGL and links no comctl32, so the declaration would be inert.
      That file was correctly deleted with its client in bacchus#138; this is
      a new file for a different purpose, not a restored one.
    - dpiAware/dpiAwareness. Fyne's GLFW driver sets DPI awareness through the
      API at startup; declaring it here too would be a second authority on the
      same setting, and the manifest wins over the API call.
    - supportedOS compatibility GUIDs. They change what GetVersionEx and a few
      behaviour shims report; nothing in this client asks.
-->
<assembly xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1" manifestVersion="1.0">
  <assemblyIdentity
      type="win32"
      name="io.github.bacchus-vpn.bacchus"
      version="1.0.0.0"
      processorArchitecture="*"/>
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges>
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="requireAdministrator" uiAccess="false"/>
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
</assembly>
